    "User requested original IMAP label boxes, baselines, abbreviations, and line breaks; current frozen percentages replace historical numbers in those original locations.",
    "User-requested panel letters without trailing periods; preserve letter case, font, size, and anchors.",
    "User-requested wording-only revision, 7 September 2026. Longer labels may wrap or use text-specific fit adjustments; scientific inputs, values, gates, colors, markers and axes remain unchanged.",
    "September 7 follow-up: Musc uses the original IMAP label box and baselines; non-IMAP displays use Muscularis. Gate assignments and percentages are unchanged.",
    "October 15 author-approved replacement: E shows whole-section P14 per 10,000 non-P14 cells and F shows log2 P14 gate enrichment from the approved A/B candidate. Four DMSO and five RARi biological replicates are circles, with mouse means and SEM. Frozen experiment-adjusted OLS P values and five-gate BH q values are displayed only when significant, with matching stars. These replace the previous two-subplot E; no analysis is rerun.",
    "October 15 author-approved relabeling: the former F IMAP is G. Frozen equal-mouse mean P14 densities, gate percentages, 0-13 shared scale, vector geometry, label boxes and axes retain their values and positions. Explanatory footers are removed from the artwork and described in the figure caption. Main A-D are unchanged.",
    "October 15 label cleanup: remove sample-size labels from the E/F treatment legend and G condition headings, and remove E/F titles. Sample sizes remain in the caption; all data, axes, statistics and panel anchors are unchanged.",
    "October 15 alignment revision supersedes earlier fixed display anchors: E is the P14 IMAP and G is whole-section abundance. B is 193.34 pt wide (26.3% larger linearly) with its native field, overlay and 200-µm calibration retained. Top-row image tops, bottoms and scale-bar baselines, scatter axes/colorbars, map zooms/colorbars and paired IMAP axes align on explicit shared baselines. Statistical ticks and annotations are 7 pt and axis labels 7.5 pt. Original data, tests, fields, densities, gates and within-map label geometry remain unchanged.",
    "Author correction: physically place abundance at upper-right E, IMAPs at lower-left F, and enrichment at lower-right G directly beneath E. The IMAP pair is side by side at the same aspect ratio, with unchanged relative gate-label geometry, source values and density scale; a shared axis label removes repetition. E and G share left/right edges. G category labels wrap to fit. A-D are pixel-identical to the preceding aligned export.",
    "Author-requested E/F/G size polish: E contracts to 128x120 pt; G widens to 176 pt beneath the same column center. F narrows to two 152-pt-wide maps with unchanged height, relative gate positions and a fixed readable 5.7-pt label font. Replicate dot area in E/G increases from 11.5 to 25 pt² without changing values, jitter, summaries, tests or colors. A-D and Extended Figure 4 remain unchanged."
